> Use dashi instead of vegetable broth for more traditional miso soup.
> Use silken tofu instead of firm tofu for more traditional miso soup.

Place @vegetable broth{4%cups} in a #medium sauce pan{} and bring to a low simmer.

In the meantime, place @white or yellow miso paste{3-4%Tbsp} (starting with lesser end of range) into a #small bowl{}, add a little hot water and whisk until smooth. This will ensure it doesn't clump when added to the soup later. Set aside.

To the broth add @green chard or other sturdy green{1/2%cup}(chopped), @green onion{1/2%cup}(chopped), and @firm tofu{1/4%cup}(cubed) (if using silken, add at the end of cooking) and cook for ~{5%minutes}. Then add @?nori{1%sheet}(cut into large rectangles) and stir. Remove from heat, add miso mixture, and stir to combine.

Taste and add more miso or a pinch of @?sea salt{} if desired. Serve warm. Best when fresh.